<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

<p>
  Last updated on 4 November 2026.
</p>

<h3>Information we collect via this website</h3>

<p>
  Browsing the site and using the map doesn't require an account, and we don't collect any
  personal information about you while you do.
</p>

<p>
  To see which areas and problems people find useful, we count page views: for each day, how
  many times the home page, each area page, each problem page and the map were opened. We only
  keep those daily totals. We don't record your IP address, set a cookie, or store anything
  that could identify you or link your visits together, and we don't use any outside analytics
  service.
</p>

<p>
  To find and fix problems with the site, we use <a href="https://www.bugsnag.com">Bugsnag</a>
  (run by SmartBear) for error monitoring. Technical details are sent to Bugsnag only when
  something goes wrong: the page address, your browser and device type, and details of the
  error. We don't include your IP address in these reports, we don't store any identifier on
  your device, and we don't use this information to track you.
</p>

<h3>When you contribute or report a mistake</h3>

<p>If you send us a contribution or a problem report, we keep what you submit:</p>
<ul>
  <li>your name and email address, if you give them (both are optional)</li>
  <li>your comment, and any problem name or links you add</li>
  <li>any photo you upload and the line you draw on it</li>
  <li>the location you give for the problem, which may be filled in from your photo's GPS data</li>
</ul>

<p>
  We use your email address only to tell you that we've received your submission and whether it
  was accepted. It is never shown on the site or shared with anyone. If you give a name, it may
  appear on the contributors leaderboard on the mapping page. Accepted photos, lines and locations
  are published on the site as part of the guide.
</p>

<p>
  To have your details removed, email hello@bowda.rocks.
</p>

<h3>Information stored on your device</h3>

<p>If you use offline mode or install Bowda as an app, your browser keeps:</p>
<ul>
  <li>the areas you have saved for offline use (maps, topos and photos)</li>
  <li>any problem reports you write while offline, until they can be sent</li>
</ul>

<p>
  Saved areas are <strong>stored only on your device</strong>. Reports written offline are sent
  to us automatically once you are back online, just as if you had submitted them online.
</p>

<h3>Your Consent</h3>

<p>
  By using Bowda, you consent to our privacy policy.
</p>

<h3>Cookie Policy</h3>
<p>
  We don't store any personal data via cookies, and we don't use any external cookies.
</p>

<h3>Contacting Us</h3>
<p>
  If you have questions regarding this privacy policy, you may email hello@bowda.rocks.
</p>